<speak>I learned that on our last trip. I thought I could deal with some calls while waiting around, but every waiting area turned out to be noisy, or the announcement came just as someone started speaking. This time I kept travel days clear of appointments. We went with the family, and it was much more enjoyable once I stopped treating the gaps as spare office time. I still checked messages briefly, but I didn't spend the whole journey with a notebook balanced on my knee.</speak>